 "source": {
  "text": "//@version=6\nindicator(\"UCTPROBE_VW_MINTICK\", overlay = false)\n\n// ─── 2026-09-27 VOCABULARY WAVE — `syminfo.mintick` PER SYMBOL ───────────────\n//\n// `syminfo.mintick` is the first vocabulary wall of two corpus scripts\n// (`chart-champions-part-1-npoc-levels-vwaps__wdeUFJ4ZD2` — `f_round_up_to_tick`;\n// `renko-candles-overlay__d76a18d49e` — `math.max(..., syminfo.mintick)`) and it\n// sits inside two more. It is not a Pine SEMANTICS question — it is a DATA value\n// this engine does not hold (`symbolScope.json::unserved`). Before any serving\n// rule can be proposed, the vendor's own value is needed across price regimes:\n//\n//   M01  syminfo.mintick            M02  syminfo.pricescale / syminfo.minmove\n//   M03  close (to see which price regime the value belongs to)\n//\n// ⛔ CAPTURE ON EACH, 1D, a handful of bars is enough (the value is per symbol,\n// not per bar — but read ≥ 5 bars so a per-bar change would show):\n//   AMEX:SPY · NASDAQ:AAPL · a sub-$1 US listing (e.g. any OTC/penny name the\n//   rig can load) · a $1–$5 name · NYSE:BRK.A · an index (SP:SPX) · a future\n//   (CME_MINI:ES1!) · a forex pair (FX:EURUSD) · BINANCE:BTCUSDT.\n// The rule a proposal would need is \"which symbols get 0.01\"; this is the list.\n\nplot(bar_index, \"M00_bar_index_CONTROL\")\nplot(syminfo.mintick, \"M01_mintick\")\nplot(syminfo.pricescale / syminfo.minmove, \"M02_pricescale_over_minmove\")\nplot(close, \"M03_close\")\n",
